<p>Nasrallah Abu Siyam, a 19-year-old Palestinian American, was shot and killed in the village of Mukhmas in the Israeli-occupied West Bank, according to Palestinian health officials and witnesses. His death has renewed scrutiny of settler-related violence in the West Bank, and his family is calling for accountability and clear answers about who was responsible.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/zRNNNsFD80HAIToUYONeZ97VWCOWb8MZttfmAVN8l3veYwcq7KEy7xx1iXtcAi29itpqDtNGqc-70z2TE_L3XP6SrpY8XRbk7JexfxR2bASkjDIjSHjdt9mLEqsTiuHB678QTNBBL9rgWvU59JqWPrIMy_s3E1Nm9rhqi4YWajZhH6ce31HA9x8cCbqtLYSYmapTrqRCqrcXIS9mq4o' alt='The funeral of Nasrallah Abu Siyam, 19, in Mukhmas, a village in the West Bank, on Thursday, a day after he was killed.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Rising violence: The New York Times said the shooting comes amid a rise in violent settler attacks in the Israeli-occupied West Bank.</li><li>US citizens: The BBC reported Abu Siyam was the sixth American citizen killed by Israeli settlers or soldiers in the West Bank in the last two years.</li><li>UN allegations: The UN human rights office accused Israel of war crimes, The Guardian reported.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Palestinian health ministry: Palestinian health officials said someone shot Nasrallah Abu Siyam dead during the incident in Mukhmas. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/20/world/middleeast/palestinian-american-teenager-killed-west-bank.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Local witness (Mukhmas resident): A resident said settlers entered the village and attacked a farmer. The shooting happened during clashes after residents intervened. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/20/israeli-settlers-west-bank-kill-palestinian-american-man'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Abu Siyam family: Relatives demanded accountability for his killing and pressed for clear answers about who was responsible. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvgk7z15gnpo'>BBC News</a>)</l